-  "description": "<p>The empirical relation a<sub>0</sub> = &kappa; c &radic;(G &rho;<sub>&Lambda;</sub>) with &kappa; &asymp; 1/2 (measured 0.465 &plusmn; 0.076 from the baryonic Tully-Fisher intercept and 0.551 &plusmn; 0.043 by a distance-free estimator) has never been derived. We ask whether the covariant candidate action of the de Sitter-MOND closure programme (a khronometric clock, a dynamical MOND scalar with a bounded-boost kernel, and a coherence operator) can relate a<sub>0</sub> to &Lambda; at all, and answer in the negative with a theorem and three computed dead ends. (i) The MOND primitive enters the static field equations only through its derivative and the FLRW background only through &Lambda; + (2&minus;K<sub>B</sub>)J(0)/2 + K(Q<sub>0</sub>)/2: with &Lambda; explicit, no equation of the action relates the two scales (a normalisation zero mode). (ii) Deleting &Lambda; and fixing the primitive's zero by an empty Newtonian vacuum yields a <em>negative</em> vacuum energy of 0.4-0.7% of &rho;<sub>&Lambda;</sub>; the constant 4&pi;<sup>4</sup>/15 of the RAR primitive that would give &kappa; &asymp; 1 belongs to the unsaturated branch the bounded-boost theorem forbids. (iii) A sequestering-type global constraint tying &Lambda; to the spacetime average of the scalar's Lagrangian misses by five orders of magnitude today and tends to zero in the de Sitter future. (iv) Promoting a<sub>0</sub> to a conserved four-form flux reverses the sign, makes a<sub>0</sub> &prop; &radic;(G&rho;<sub>&Lambda;</sub>) structural with the flux amplitude cancelling, and leaves the coefficient as the coupling ratio Z/&beta;<sup>2</sup> = 7.96; the induced environmental a<sub>0</sub> is invisible in galaxies, switches the scalar off above 155 a<sub>0</sub>, and shifts the Gaia DR4 wide-binary boost at 2 kAU by &minus;0.019, about one sigma. On the observable side the only coefficient-free alternative left standing, the horizon form a<sub>0</sub> = c<sup>2</sup>/(2&pi; L<sub>dS</sub>) with &kappa; = 0.461, is separated from 1/2 by 8.5%, below the 9.5% mass-budget floor of the Tully-Fisher route, and is exactly degenerate with the H<sub>0</sub> tension: &kappa; = 1/2 on the Planck H<sub>0</sub> and &kappa; = 0.461 on the SH0ES H<sub>0</sub> predict the same a<sub>0</sub> to 0.2%. We conclude that &kappa; = 1/2 is an empirical boundary condition that this class of local actions cannot derive, and that its determination is a precision problem gated by the stellar mass-to-light zero point, the absolute gas scale and H<sub>0</sub>. Every number is produced by a committed script with checks that can fail (kappa_closure/k01-k04 in the public repository). AI-assisted research draft; not peer reviewed.</p>",
